The boot pool's own node stays a root rather than hanging below its block,
so an Untyped covers a pool that does not lie below it,
and revoking below that Untyped would not reach the root task's objects:
the demo's successor cannot end the root task.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: memory that may hold kernel objects overlaps a node not above or below it

diff --git a/kernel/boot.c b/kernel/boot.c
--- a/kernel/boot.c
+++ b/kernel/boot.c
@@ -70,7 +70,6 @@ struct thread *boot_create_root(void)
         cap_store(table, BOOT_CAP_POOL_RAM, &pool_ram, root_ram) != KERR_OK) {
         kpanic("cannot fill the root task's table");
     }
-    cap_attach(&table->slots[BOOT_CAP_POOL_RAM], &pool->node);
 
